
# ⚡ FocusFlow – Productivity Dashboard

A modern, dark-themed productivity dashboard designed to help users manage daily tasks, track progress, and improve focus using a Pomodoro timer.

## 🚀 Features

- **Task Management:** Add, complete, and delete daily tasks.
- **Progress Tracking:** Automatically calculates completed tasks and productivity percentage.
- **Pomodoro Timer:** Built-in 25-minute focus timer.
- **Data Persistence:** Tasks are saved automatically using Local Storage.
- **Responsive Design:** Works on desktop and mobile devices.
- **Dark UI:** Clean and modern user interface.

## 🛠️ Technologies Used

- HTML5 – Structure
- CSS3 – Styling and responsive design
- JavaScript – Functionality and interactivity
- Local Storage – Saving user tasks

## 📸 Project Preview

Open `index.html` in your browser to explore the dashboard.

## 📂 Project Structure

```text
FocusFlow/
│
└── index.html
```

## ⚙️ How to Run

1. Clone this repository:

   ```bash
   git clone https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/FocusFlow-Productivity-Dashboard.git
   ```

2. Open the project folder.
3. Open `index.html` in your browser.
4. Start managing your tasks!

## 🎯 Project Objective

The main objective of FocusFlow is to create a simple and efficient productivity tool that helps users organize their daily activities, monitor task completion, and maintain focus through time management.

## 🔮 Future Improvements

- User authentication
- Daily and weekly productivity analytics
- Customizable focus sessions
- Task deadlines and reminders
- Sound notifications
- Cloud-based data storage

